Produce the Number of Parts You Need
For the plant you are modeling you can produce the number of parts you need.
To produce a certain number of MUs during the interval you define:
• Select Time of Creation > Number Adjustable.
Video on YouTube
10-166 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• Enter the Amount, i.e., the number of MUs to be created.
• Select the Creation Times, which determine the points in time at which the Source creates the MUs.
Select a distribution from the drop-down list Creation Times and enter the values that the distribution
requires into the text box.
The Source produces the number of MUs at the different times which the random number generator
generated at the beginning of the simulation. The determined times are contained within the bounds if
you enter a lower bound and an upper bound.
If you select a Constant time, the Source creates the number of MUs all at one point in time.
Note
If you set the Creation Times via SimTalk, use the attribute Interval.
Note
For the setting Number Adjustable you cannot select the MU Selection > Sequence.
• Click OK.
If you select Time of Creation > Interval Adjustable or Time of Creation > Number Adjustable you can
also select how the Source produces which types of MUs.
Produce the Number of Parts You Need
